[09:06:26] STORY-API-005 is complete.
[09:06:26] ## Resumed, not restarted
[09:06:26] The interrupted attempt had already written the controller, the variant mapping, the 16-test contract suite and the Spring wiring, but had run no tests and updated no documentation or result records. I verified the existing work by running the suites, then completed the rest.
[09:06:26] ## What the endpoint does
[09:06:26] `POST /api/prices/refresh` with a required `variant` (`PROFIT` or `DISCOVERY`) submits exactly one invocation of the matching `TradingPostPriceRefreshService` method as a background task, returning 202 with `taskId`, the variant's operation key, `statusUrl` and a `Location` header. The existing `GET /api/sync/tasks/{taskId}` reports the outcome — no new status route. There is deliberately no combined "all prices" value; `ALL` is rejected by the same rule as a typo, with a test asserting it so the absence is recorded rather than accidental.
[09:06:26] ## The key choice, made on evidence
[09:06:26] Two operation keys (`PRICE_REFRESH_PROFIT`, `PRICE_REFRESH_DISCOVERY`), checked against the actual shared write rather than by analogy: both variants write `tp_prices` via `INSERT … ON CONFLICT (item_id) DO UPDATE`, with no `DELETE` anywhere on the path (`sync/TpSync.java:78-89`). Overlapping runs can only overwrite a row with another fresh quote for the same item — and that concurrency is already reachable from the two JavaFX buttons today, so a single shared key would have been a new restriction, not a preserved behavior. No user decision was warranted; no scheduling or cross-operation exclusion added.
[09:06:26] ## Tests run
[09:06:26] - **Default `./mvnw test`: 262 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors** (246 pre-existing unchanged + 16 new) — counts read from `target/surefire-reports`, not the exit code.
[09:06:26] - `CraftingProfitViewTpRefreshIT` + `CraftingDiscoveryViewTpRefreshIT`: 4 pass — both JavaFX refresh buttons unchanged in process.
[09:06:26] - Both calculation real-DB equivalence ITs: 4 pass.
[09:06:26] - `CraftingProfitApiRealDbPerfIT`: pass, max **1794 ms** (3151 rows, 1,305,944 bytes) — same band as the previous two stories, far inside §33's budget. Backend request time only, not full-page proof.
[09:06:26] - Live against a running server: every rejection with its exact message, 405/404 from the framework, the account and global triggers' messages unchanged, and the profit calculation still 200.
[09:06:26] ## Two contract facts stated rather than hidden
[09:06:26] A succeeded task does **not** mean prices were fetched — the ten-minute freshness filter can select nothing. A failed task says nothing about how much was written — the refresh commits per batch, which is exactly what the existing no-rollback wording claims and no more.
[09:06:26] Docs updated at their owners: `CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE.md` (§2/§3/§4, new §5.9), `TEST_STRATEGY.md` §35.3, `KNOWN_PROBLEMS.md` §7.10. Story file, `BACKLOG.md` and `CLAUDE_RESULT.md` record the result.
[09:06:26] **Not done, by scope:** the accepted path was never triggered against the live GW2 API — it would fetch commerce quotes and upsert your real `tp_prices`. Milestone closure stays with planning; `STORY-QUALITY-004` (the bounded Phase 4 health review) remains open.
