[21:12:38] STORY-API-006 is complete.
[21:12:38] ## What changed
[21:12:38] New read-only route `GET /api/crafting/selector-options`, over the existing `application.CharacterSelectionService` — the same read both JavaFX selectors already use. I checked the five Phase 4 routes first: they all *consume* a scope, none reads one, so there was no equivalent route to reuse.
[21:12:38] | File | Change |
[21:12:38] |---|---|
[21:12:38] | `web/CraftingSelectorOptionsApiController.java` | new — one `GET`, no body/parameter; one service call + one `map` |
[21:12:38] | `web/dto/CraftingSelectorOptionsResponse.java` | new — transport record, primitives and strings only |
[21:12:38] | `web/CraftingSelectorOptionsApiExceptionHandler.java` | new — 503 / 500, both messages fixed |
[21:12:38] | `web/Gw2ApiApplication.java` | one shared `CharacterSelectionService` bean |
[21:12:38] | `test/web/CraftingSelectorOptionsApiControllerTest.java` | new — 7 contract tests |
[21:12:38] | `test/web/Gw2ApiApplicationBootTest.java` | one wiring assertion |
[21:12:38] | `docs/CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE.md` | §2 layout, §3 package row, §4 diagram, new §5.10 |
[21:12:38] Response: `defaultScopeKind`, `disciplines`, `characterOptionCount`, `characterOptions[{characterName, discipline, rating, active}]`. The controller queries no repository and applies no sort/filter/dedup/eligibility rule, so the service's values and order arrive verbatim; `repo.CharacterRepository.DiscRow` is read to copy it, never serialized.
[21:12:38] `SQLException` → 503 `DATA_STORE_UNAVAILABLE` with the same code and message as the calculation routes; anything else → 500 `SELECTOR_OPTIONS_FAILED`. It's a separate advice for the reason `SyncApiExceptionHandler` already records — `ApiExceptionHandler`'s 500 says a *calculation* failed, which is wrong here, and I didn't reword that established contract.
[21:12:38] ## Two judgment calls (documented at §5.10)
[21:12:38] 1. **The nine generic disciplines are in the response**, mirrored in the controller. Otherwise the browser could only offer disciplines someone happens to have synced — i.e. it would reproduce the list itself, which AC 1/3 exist to prevent. It's the JavaFX view's presentation list, not a service fact, so it's mirrored exactly as STORY-API-001 mirrored that view's setting defaults. `defaultScopeKind` reads `CraftingProfitApiMapper.DEFAULT_SCOPE_KIND`, so the two routes can't disagree about `ALL`.
[21:12:38] 2. **`active` is reported, not dropped** — a service-provided fact the caller can't re-derive; no rule applied to it.
[21:12:38] ## Tests run
[21:12:38] `./mvnw test` on the final tree: **270 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**. Targeted run of `web.*Test` + `application.CharacterSelectionServiceTest`: 97 pass, including the unchanged Profit (17) and Discovery (20) contract tests. The 7 new tests cover preserved values/order/count; option JSON field names asserted to be exactly the four documented ones; a returned option fed through `CraftingProfitApiMapper.toEffective(...)` proving it yields `DiscChoice.CHAR_DISCIPLINE` with the same values; empty database → 200, count 0, no invented character; 503 asserted free of `jdbc`/credentials; 500 asserted free of SQL/exception text; unknown sub-path still 404.
[21:12:38] ## Remaining uncertainty
[21:12:38] - Never exercised against a real database or running server — the contract tests stub the service, as the other route tests do. No `*RealDbIT` added: the read is one existing `SELECT` already covered by the JavaFX ITs.
[21:12:38] - The JavaFX selector ITs weren't re-run (desktop session + Postgres required); no file they touch changed.
[21:12:38] - If the JavaFX base discipline list is ever edited, `GENERIC_DISCIPLINES` must be edited with it. Nothing enforces that — the cost of mirroring rather than relocating a JavaFX presentation constant.
[21:12:38] Story file, `BACKLOG.md` and `CLAUDE_RESULT.md` updated; no milestone or phase transition declared.
